waymap for Debian/Kali Linux
============================

This package contains waymap, an advanced web application security scanner
with AI-powered vulnerability analysis.

Installation
------------
Install the package using:

    sudo apt install waymap

Configuration
-------------
Configuration files are stored in /etc/waymap. You can create a secrets.json
file to store API keys for SerpApi and WPScan:

    {
      "serpapi_api_key": "YOUR_SERPAPI_KEY",
      "wpscan_api_token": "YOUR_WPSCAN_TOKEN"
    }

Alternatively, you can use environment variables:
- SERPAPI_API_KEY for Google dork discovery
- WPSCAN_API_TOKEN for WordPress scanning

Usage
-----
Basic usage:

    waymap --target https://example.com --scan xss

For more information, see the man page:

    man waymap

Or run:

    waymap --help

Legal
-----
Waymap is intended for authorized security testing and educational use only.
Only scan systems you own or have explicit permission to test.

The authors are not responsible for misuse.

Building from Source
---------------------
To build this package from source, ensure you have the necessary build
dependencies:

    sudo apt build-dep waymap

Then build the package:

    dpkg-buildpackage -us -uc

Reporting Bugs
--------------
Report bugs at: https://github.com/TrixSec/waymap/issues

For Debian-specific issues, you may also file a bug in the Debian Bug
Tracking System.
